<title>FRANCE: French health spending slips slightly in October.</title>
<headline>French health spending slips slightly in October.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CNAM French health insurance fund said it spent 37.987 billion francs in October, a figure which is 0.1 percent lower than in September and 0.2 percent lower than in October 1995.</p>
<p>Spending for the year to October stood at 365.661 billion francs.</p>
<p>The French government aims to keep health spending within a limit of 2.1 percent growth in 1996.</p>
<p>The CNAM said that spending sofar this year was at the same level as in 1995.</p>
</text>
